post_install() {
  cat <<'EOM'
GambiarraInfinite V4 (Linux port) installed.

  Launcher : gambiarra-infinite
  Menu     : "GambiarraInfinite V4"

The app drives the GambiarraInfinite CLI over a local service; it is bundled with
this package, so nothing else needs to be installed. That CLI is the Gambiarra
fork of OpenCode (with the /_larpcode/* API: GambiarraAPI Marketplace,
jailbreaks, images, free-route and Tor), not the stock upstream CLI.

Upgrading from a build that shipped the stock OpenCode CLI? Quit the app once and
relaunch: it notices the version mismatch, stops the old background service and
starts the bundled Gambiarra CLI.
EOM
}

post_upgrade() {
  post_install
}

pre_remove() {
  cat <<'EOM'
GambiarraInfinite V4 removed.
Config/data stays in ~/.config/ai.larpcode.desktop.dev if you want to clean it.
EOM
}